Step 1: Create a Discord Application
https://discord.com/developers/
Log in and click "New Application".
Enter a name for your app and click "Create".
Step 2: Add a Bot to Your Application
In your app, navigate to the "Bot" section.
Click "Add Bot" and confirm by selecting "Yes, do it!".
Grant the bot all necessary text and read permissions.
Copy the Bot Token.
Step 3: Configure OAuth2 and Generate an Invite Link
Go to the "OAuth2" section and click "URL Generator".
Select the following scopes:
bot
applications.commands
Grant relevant permissions for the bot.
Copy the generated OAuth2 URL.
Open a new browser tab, paste the URL, and follow the prompts to grant access to Discord channels.
Step 4: Create a Discord Server and Connect the Bot
In Discord, click the "+" icon on the left sidebar to create a new server.
Once the server is set up, the bot will automatically connect to it if you've followed the previous steps correctly.
This process will allow your bot to read and send messages in your Discord server.
